[agent] I've investigated the interface thoroughly and must give up cleanly. Here is my report.
[agent] ## Result: interface is missing the required capability
[agent] **The task cannot be completed through the interface under test.**
[agent] ### What the task requires
[agent] A Vertex AI **Feature Store online serving** flow: register `data/features.csv` as a feature table/view (`profilesaf22bf`, v1, record key `account_id`), stand up a **Feature Online Store**, enable **online/low-latency serving**, and read each key's feature vector through the **online read path** (`FetchFeatureValues`).
[agent] ### What the allowed interface actually exposes
[agent] The permitted CLI surface is `gcloud {ai, auth, config, components, storage, monitoring}` plus `bq`. In this gcloud version (573.0.0), the **GA `gcloud ai`** group contains only:
[agent] ```
[agent] custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index-endpoints, indexes,
[agent] model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations,
[agent] persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs
[agent] ```
[agent] There is **no** `feature-online-stores`, `feature-groups`, `feature-views`, `feature-registries`, or legacy `featurestores` group — I verified each returns `Invalid choice`. All Vertex AI Feature Store commands (both the legacy Featurestore API and the current Feature Registry / Feature Online Store APIs) live **only under `gcloud beta ai` / `gcloud alpha ai`**, and both `beta` and `alpha` are hard-blocked by the environment's allowlist:
[agent] > `DENIED: … gcloud beta is off-interface.`
[agent] ### Why there's no workaround within the rules
[agent] - `bq` can load the CSV into the BigQuery dataset, but that is the **offline store** — the task explicitly forbids reading from the CSV or the offline store, and requires the **online/low-latency** path.
[agent] - Enabling online serving and performing an online `FetchFeatureValues` fetch requires the Feature Online Store / Feature View APIs, which are not reachable via any allowed `gcloud ai` (GA) command, `bq`, `storage`, or `monitoring`.
[agent] - Local Python/SDK/`curl`/REST are all blocked (CLI mode), so there is no permitted route to the online serving API.
[agent] ### Missing capability (the measurement)
[agent] **The GA `gcloud ai` CLI exposes no Vertex AI Feature Store / Feature Online Store / Feature View surface at all.** Online feature-serving setup and reads are only available through `gcloud beta`/`gcloud alpha` (blocked here) or the client SDK/REST (blocked in CLI mode). With the interface restricted to GA `gcloud ai` + `bq`, there is no way to enable online/low-latency serving or to read a feature vector through the online path, so `submission/answers.json` cannot be produced on the platform. No partial resources were created.
